1. Her name is Elias Delaria, and she is a British VTuber. (Verbatim: "My name is Elias Delaria, British VTuber, not a goose.")
2. She has a brother named Theo, who is referred to as "Ellibro" during streams. (Verbatim: "Hello, my name is Theo. Ellibro.")
3. She struggles with sleep and has irregular sleeping patterns, often falling asleep during the day. (Verbatim: "I've been asleep most of the day, to be honest. My sleeping patterns worked.")
4. She typically goes to bed around half past nine in the evening. (Verbatim: "It's half nine, man. I'm usually in bed in half an hour.")
5. Her standard greeting and sign-off line is "I hope everyone's having a lovely day, a great afternoon, morning, evening, goodnight, wherever you are!" (Verbatim: "I hope everyone's having a lovely day, a great afternoon, morning, evening, goodnight, wherever you are!")
6. She used to use her current catchphrase only as an outro before switching to using it both at the beginning and end of streams. (Verbatim: "I used to say it as an outro. Oh, I use it for both.")
7. She grew up being bullied, which made her self-conscious about pronunciation and speaking. (Verbatim: "Yeah, I grew up being made fun of it, so I'm not self-conscious of that or anything.")
8. She has read the manga for *The Promised Neverland* up to the end of the first season but chose not to watch the second season. (Verbatim: "I read the manga up to where the first season ended.")
9. She dislikes *The Promised Neverland* Season 2 and agrees it was poorly made, comparing it negatively to a "PowerPoint presentation." (Verbatim: "It was so fucking pointless, it made no sense!... It was like watching a PowerPoint presentation.")
10. She has not yet debuted as a VTuber with a full model and is currently using a temporary image, possibly making her a "PNGTuber" for now. (Verbatim: "I'm not debuting any time soon, so it's not like...") [end of text]



1. She has a strong preference for "trash isekai" anime, particularly those featuring an overpowered protagonist who is underestimated and then proves others wrong. (Verbatim: "the reason why i like my trash isekais is because they have the same trope of like an op protagonist that's like underestimated and then proves everybody wrong")

2. She enjoys villainess-themed manhwa, especially stories where the protagonist is reincarnated or looped back in time to change their fate. (Verbatim: "i just like my villainess manhwa okay like give me give me a villainess like or thrown back in time trying to change her fate like that")

3. She likes shoujo anime but avoids emotionally intense ones like *Kimini Tadoke* because they make her feel sad and increase feelings of loneliness. (Verbatim: "i really want to watch kiminitadoke okay but i don't want to feel sad i don't want to watch it and be like so i haven't")

4. She is inspired by shounen or sports anime that depict characters striving to do their best despite adversity, such as *Haikyuu!!*. (Verbatim: "when i watch like is it haiku always inspires me because i'm like look at him trying to fight the fact that he's short... i want to try because like i love the idea of being spiteful towards the world and being like i'm gonna give it my best")

5. She compares her anime-watching habits to her real-life eating habits, preferring familiar, comforting choices like a chicken burger she orders repeatedly. (Verbatim: "it's kind of reflective of how i eat food irl okay i'm the kind of person that will order the same meal from from the same place... i'll be like yo i want a chicken burger")

6. She occasionally tries new things but finds it rare and sometimes regrettable, often reverting to her usual preferences. (Verbatim: "occasionally very occasionally i'll try like something different and be like oh i don't want to have a chicken burger today i'm going to have like something else and that is quite rare")

7. She finds it difficult and scary to recommend anime to others, especially because her taste includes "trash" she enjoys despite knowing it may not be objectively good. (Verbatim: "i find it so scary recommending anime to people... i'll be like oh i'll be honest i like i i watch trash like just because i watch something doesn't mean it's good")

8. She believes in starting new anime viewers with upper-mid-tier shows rather than masterpieces like *Full Metal Alchemist: Brotherhood* to avoid setting unreasonably high expectations. (Verbatim: "don't start them off with the best one don't don't set them off on the peak because then everything after the peak will be disappointment")

9. She enjoys "cute" content like JP McDonald's ads but notes they have a "lonely cute" vibe that can affect her mood. (Verbatim: "the jp mcdonald's ads are cute but they're lonely cute")

10. She expresses interest in future content discussions on her channel, such as dedicated talks about isekai or manhwa. (Verbatim: "oh i should do a whole talk on like isekais yeah yeah there are so many different topics of anime that can be covered") [end of text]



1. She was in university and had experiences related to anime discussions during that time. (Verbatim: "this was at university um and the anime she decided to watch was uh was killer kill")

2. She finds *School Days* deeply shocking and traumatizing, especially since she watched it when she was young. (Verbatim: "school days is wild though school days i will never recover fully from the shock i was really young when i watched it")

3. She got into *School Days* because it was listed near *School Rumble*, which she enjoyed as a light-hearted school comedy. (Verbatim: "i was really sad it ended and then i was like oh okay the next on this list is like alphabetically like above it there was school days")

4. She believes *Killer Queen* (likely meant *Killer Killer* or similar) is not a beginner-friendly anime due to its satirical take on anime tropes. (Verbatim: "i wouldn't recommend gintama because because it's like the references in it right like gintama is great but it's for later on")

5. She dislikes certain types of "cringe" anime, especially those involving overly close sibling relationships. (Verbatim: "no don't watch oromo of your siblings no that's cringe that's cringe")

6. She has a critical view of ecchi anime tropes, particularly the unrealistic physics of character animations. (Verbatim: "golden boy was wild and i didn't realize like yeah it's about like a i.t company and it's like a all women i.t company")

7. She finds anime fashion unrealistic and questions the comfort of characters' outfits, especially high heels and tight dresses in work settings. (Verbatim: "the first thing i thought when i was watching golden boy was like there's no way she's hecking comfortable wearing what she's wearing")

8. She values realism in anime, such as characters changing outfits, and appreciates attention to detail. (Verbatim: "one thing i do love though is when animes actually change their outfits")

9. She was not socially active or "cool" in school and was focused on studying instead. (Verbatim: "i wasn't cool at school at all and i was just focused on studying")

10. Watching school romance anime makes her feel old, especially when characters are underage. (Verbatim: "it makes me feel old as heck i'm like what the heck you're all 14 13 like you heckin children") [end of text]



1. She worked as a software developer before or alongside her VTubing career, primarily using C#. (Verbatim: "as a developer i was working in c sharp")

2. Her formal education background is in Python programming. (Verbatim: "my education is in python")

3. She used to work from home as a developer and appreciated having background voices for company. (Verbatim: "i used to like having a background voice when i used to work at home um as a developer")

4. She has a history of being very quiet growing up, raised in a quiet household. (Verbatim: "i was very quiet and what i've realized is um... if you're raised in a household which is quiet okay you will most likely like get a more nasal voice")

5. She was raised to believe she should only speak when spoken to, leading to suppressed communication. (Verbatim: "i was a girl that was always told only speak when you're spoken to okay")

6. She considers herself a "yapper" and attributes her talkativeness to making up for years of silence. (Verbatim: "i gotta make up for all that time all those heckin times growing up like the backlog is real")

7. Her longest continuous talking session was about 23 hours, lasting through her birthday. (Verbatim: "my longest yap session was about like 23 hours and then i fell asleep for a bit and that was my last birthday")

8. She dislikes how high school is portrayed as the "best days of your life," calling it a lie. (Verbatim: "whoever said high school is the best days of your life they was lying")

9. She felt socially isolated during her youth and primarily spent time studying, watching anime, and playing video games. (Verbatim: "coming back from like summer holidays and being like what did you do i stayed in my room studying and watching anime and playing video game")

10. She expresses a longing for better social experiences during adolescence and finds adult life more fulfilling than high school. (Verbatim: "the most interesting thing about becoming an adult was the discovery that my years in high school were not nearly as important as i thought back then") [end of text]



1. She struggled with anxiety and overthinking, especially about speaking in public. (Verbatim: "speaking is difficult when you're really held down by a whole ton of overthinking and a lot of worry like all the worry in the world.")

2. She was very quiet in school despite being academically capable. (Verbatim: "every single time it was always the same same same same thing on repeat oh yeah your daughter's really good but she's really quiet in class and it'd be really nice if she spoke up.")

3. She avoided participating in class because she feared giving wrong answers and being mocked. (Verbatim: "i was too worried the answer was wrong because like oh my gosh i literally would feel like just taking straight up dying you've put your hand up and you've confidently answered the question and they're like no.")

4. A teacher once mocked her correct answer about capitalizing "I," causing her to cry. (Verbatim: "i put my hand up and i was like oh i you know like when you're writing a sentence and you write i as a word is always a capital i and then the teacher made fun of me... then she laughed at me and then i cried.")

5. She attended a public Catholic school in a rough area of England. (Verbatim: "my secondary school which was like a public catholic school in ingerland in a rough area.")

6. She was extremely short during school years and had a significant growth spurt later. (Verbatim: "i was tiny in school okay i was tiny i was super tiny i had a growth spurt all right i did grow i did i doubled in height at least.")

7. She weighed about three stone (42 pounds or 19 kilograms) during her school years. (Verbatim: "i weighed about three stone back in school yeah so about 42 pounds 19 kilos.")

8. She was too scared to use school bathrooms due to intimidating older girls. (Verbatim: "i was too scared to go to the bathroom at school because the bathroom always had really scary girls in it like i was not going to the to to the to the to the school bathrooms like heck nah.")

9. She is British and notes differences between British and American English terms. (Verbatim: "i'm british okay everything i say is gonna be in it's yeah hi hi welcome on in.")

10. She recalls a chaotic school environment with frequent fights, dangerous stunts, and high teacher turnover. (Verbatim: "we went for at least seven teachers um because they i don't know why the kids like insisted on like trying to make the teacher cry.") [end of text]



1. She was extremely small as a child, weighing about 19 kg (42 lbs or three stone) and being short enough for people to pick her up and spin her around. (Verbatim: "I was about i was three stone so about 42 pounds 19 kilos yeah i was tiny i was tiny... people did like to pick me up and spin me around so yeah i guess i can see why.")

2. She experienced a significant growth spurt during her youth, transitioning from being unusually short to above average height. (Verbatim: "I had a really big growth spurt like for real... in class i was not this height.")

3. Her current height is 172 centimeters (approximately 5'7"), which she describes as slightly taller than average. (Verbatim: "I am 172 centimeters that is my uh real height... i'm like average height slightly on the taller side.")

4. She identifies as half-Asian, with her mother being Asian and small in stature, while her father is tall, which she believes explains her height. (Verbatim: "I'm half so i was pretty certain i was always gonna stay short ish like my mother is tiny so my mother is asian and she is really small... it seems i've inherited my father's height because my dad's quite tall.")

5. She has long leg length relative to her body, which affects how clothes like trousers fit her. (Verbatim: "Most of my height is my legs though like because i have a long leg length apparently for when i get trousers and stuff.")

6. During university and the pandemic, she worked jobs while attending school, interacting with colleagues virtually before meeting them in person. (Verbatim: "There was like that sort of period of time where like you'd like work with people and stuff and like this is when i was like working jobs but also at uni.")

7. People who met her virtually were often shocked by her actual height when meeting in person, sometimes insisting she must be shorter than she is. (Verbatim: "Everyone was so confused then as well... people are trying to gaslight my height.")

8. She sometimes feels self-conscious about her height, wishing she were smaller and cuter, as she associates cuteness with being short. (Verbatim: "I wish i wasn't as this tool i wish i was like a slightly cuter height... i always picture cute and small being together.")

9. She has been told by others that her “short person energy” is so strong that people don’t notice her height until she stands up. (Verbatim: "A lot of people don't notice my height when I'm with them... it's not noticeable until I stand up.")

10. At conventions, she has overheard people being intimidated by her height, including men who refused to approach her because she was taller than them. (Verbatim: "I've overheard people literally say that they're too scared to go up to me because i'm too tall... no she's taller than me.") [end of text]



